---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Something Went Wrong (500) | DocCheck"
  description="Something went wrong on our end. Your files are safe — DocCheck processes everything in your browser and uploads nothing. Try again or go back home."
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="prose error-page">
    <p class="error-code" aria-hidden="true">500</p>
    <h1>Something went wrong on our end</h1>
    <p>Sorry — the page couldn't be loaded due to a server problem. <strong>Your files are safe:</strong> DocCheck checks and fixes files inside your browser and never uploads them, so nothing of yours was sent or lost.</p>
    <div class="btn-row error-actions">
      <button type="button" class="btn-primary" onclick="window.location.reload()">Try Again</button>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/" style="text-decoration:none;text-align:center;">Go to Homepage</a>
    </div>
    <p class="fineprint">Still seeing this? Tell us what happened via the <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> page — describe the page you visited in words, without attaching personal documents.</p>
    <h2>Meanwhile, you can</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/#check">Check a photo or signature file</a></li>
      <li><a href="/requirements/">Browse all requirements</a></li>
      <li><a href="/how-it-works/">How DocCheck works</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .error-page { text-align: center; max-width: 60ch; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 0 8px; }
  .error-page h1 { margin-top: 0; }
  .error-page ul { text-align: left; }
  .error-code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 18vw, 7rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fail);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .error-actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; max-width: 480px; margin: 16px auto 0; }
  .error-actions a, .error-actions button { padding: 12px 14px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .error-actions { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
